#
# Without this the reader converts flight time to m/z with a two-point linear-in-sqrt chord that is
# -5 to -11 ppm biased (m/z dependent), costing roughly 6-11% of closed-search peptide
# identifications. This uses the vendor's own MzCalibration table from analysis.tdf instead, and
# exports BrukerTimsFile::lastMzCalibration() so the emitted file can record which path ran.
#
# Base: OpenMS/OpenMS develop bd4b89555629d68b431b189a4c841efbcc4dfeea (2026-04-24).
